  "findings": [
    {
      "text": "On [CrowS-Pairs](/evals/crows-pairs), GLM-130B shows fewer biases on almost all stereotype categories except religion and nationality versus GPT-3 and OPT-175B.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "21",
        "pdfPage": 21,
        "quote": "except for religion and nationality. We speculate that it is because GLM-130B is a bilingual"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Authors speculate bilingual English–Chinese pre-training may reconcile US-centric [CrowS-Pairs](/evals/crows-pairs) stereotypes and yield less harmful measured bias.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "21",
        "pdfPage": 21,
        "quote": "help LLMs to present less harmful biases for better fairness. Finally, we also admit that GLM-"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Authors admit GLM-130B may present special Chinese biases that lack testing benchmarks.", "tone": "mixed",
      "source": {
        "page": "21",
        "pdfPage": 21,
        "quote": "130B may in turn presents some special Chinese biases which currently lack testing benchmarks"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "On [RealToxicPrompts](https://arxiv.org/abs/2009.11462) (Figure 9), the paper reports GLM-130B has a lower continuation toxicity rate than GPT-3 Davinci in all prompt-toxicity bins, but gives no numeric rates in the text layer.", "tone": "good",
      "source": {
        "page": "23",
        "pdfPage": 23,
        "quote": "GLM-130B has a lower toxicity rate in all cases, indicating that GLM-130B is less prone to gener-"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Before granting weights, applicants must agree under the model license not to use the model for deeds harmful to society and human beings.", "tone": "neutral",
      "source": {
        "page": "21",
        "pdfPage": 21,
        "quote": "in the model license we demand them to agree that they will not use it"
      }
    }
  ],
